<title>USA: St Joseph hogs steady - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs steady - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Tuesday, barrows and gilts traded steady. Top $58.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>Rains halted field work and more hogs may move today.</p>
<p>However, not as many dirt farmers raise hogs anymore.</p>
<p>Beautiful corn planting weather Tuesday and higher prices pushed Interior Iowa movement up to 104,000. Short kills early this week and packers not needing many hogs.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    230-270 lbs	57.50-58.00</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-290 lbs	56.00-57.00</p>
<p>    US 3-4    290-310 lbs	54.00-55.00</p>
<p>Sows - steady/up $1.00. Top $41.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2     300-500 lbs    48.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3     500-550 lbs    49.00</p>
<p>		   550-700 lbs    51.00-52.00</p>
<p>Boars:	  300-700 lbs    40.00</p>
<p>		  200-300 lbs    41.00</p>
</text>
